"""The mutants. Grouped by script; each line names the property it breaks.
Sources: the independent test audit of 2026-10-11 (ids S/F/I/P/G/A/R/C/M/T/X) plus later additions.

Each is (id, file, old, new, selftest, extra args, kind). kind: "lean" when the selftest builds a
Lean fixture (mutants.py checks this); "pdf" when only a check that reads a COMPILED PDF kills it
(found by running every mutant with FORMALIZE_NO_PDF: these survived); "plain" otherwise. A new
mutant of make_report, signoff or project is "pdf" only if it survives `mutants.py --no-pdf ID`."""
import os
# the project the project-dependent selftests run against: set by mutants.py (--project NAME, or
# the project the checked-out branch selects)
PROJ = ["--project", os.environ.get("MUTANT_PROJECT", "")]
MUTANTS = []

